Description: Let modifiers tapped on their own send key combinations.
 Mutter already treats a lone tap of two modifiers specially: the overlay key opens the overview and the
 locate-pointer key shows the pointer. This adds more such keys, configured with tap-keys in
 org.gnome.mutter, which maps a modifier to the accelerator sent in its place when the modifier is pressed
 and released on its own. Pressed together with other keys it stays an ordinary modifier.
 .
 The tap detection is the one the other two keys use, including the reset on pointer buttons and the check
 for windows inhibiting shortcuts. Each tap key has its own state and sees every key event, so a tap key
 pressed while another one is held sends nothing for either. The combination is sent through a virtual
 keyboard, so keybinding processing handles it and it reaches keybindings and global shortcuts.
 .
 The test in src/tests/keybindings.c configures two tap keys and holds each together with another key, also
 with the other tap key, which must send nothing. Then it taps each on its own, which must trigger a
 keybinding bound to the combination it sends.
