+      <summary>Modifiers which send a key combination when tapped on their own</summary>
+      <description>
+        Maps a modifier key, such as "Super_R" or "Alt_L", to the key
+        combination sent in its place when it is pressed and released on its
+        own, an accelerator such as "XF86Launch9" or "&lt;Shift&gt;F24". The
+        combination is sent through a virtual keyboard, so keybinding
+        processing handles it and it triggers keybindings and global
+        shortcuts. Pressed together with other keys, the modifier stays an
+        ordinary modifier.
+        The overlay key has precedence when both name the same key.
+      </description>
+    </key>
